    <!-- PAGE 3: ASSET PROTECTION -->
    <div class="page">
        <div class="header">
            <div class="logo">Alliance Notary Solutions</div>
            <h1 class="title">Asset Protection Secrets</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">Shield Your Wealth from Creditors and Government Seizure</p>
        </div>
        
        <h2 class="section-title">The Homestead Exemption Strategy</h2>
        <div class="content">
            <p>Your primary residence can be one of your most powerful asset protection tools. In states like Florida and Texas, homestead exemptions provide unlimited protection from creditors.</p>
        </div>
        
        <ul class="bullet-list">
            <li>Move to a state with unlimited homestead exemption</li>
            <li>Pay down mortgage to build protected equity</li>
            <li>Consider upgrading to a more expensive home</li>
            <li>Establish domicile properly to qualify for protection</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h2 class="section-title">Domestic Asset Protection Trusts</h2>
        <div class="content">
            <p>Certain states allow you to be both the settlor and beneficiary of a trust while still protecting assets from creditors. These "self-settled spendthrift trusts" offer powerful protection.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="highlight-box">
            <h3>Best States for Asset Protection Trusts:</h3>
            <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0;">
                <li>✓ <strong>Nevada:</strong> 2-year statute of limitations</li>
                <li>✓ <strong>South Dakota:</strong> No state income tax on trusts</li>
                <li>✓ <strong>Delaware:</strong> Strong trust laws, business-friendly</li>
                <li>✓ <strong>Alaska:</strong> Pioneer in self-settled trusts</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        
        <h2 class="section-title">The LLC Shield Strategy</h2>
        <div class="content">
            <p>Limited Liability Companies can protect business assets and provide tax advantages when structured correctly.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="steps">
            <div class="step">Form LLC in asset-protection friendly state</div>
            <div class="step">Transfer business and investment assets to LLC</div>
            <div class="step">Elect appropriate tax treatment (S-Corp election may save self-employment tax)</div>
            <div class="step">Maintain proper corporate formalities</div>
        </div>
        
        <h2 class="section-title">Retirement Account Protection</h2>
        <div class="content">
            <p>Different retirement accounts offer varying levels of creditor protection under federal and state law.</p>
        </div>
        
        <table class="table">
            <tbody><tr>
                <th>Account Type</th>
                <th>Federal Protection</th>
                <th>Bankruptcy Protection</th>
                <th>State Varies</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>401(k)/403(b)</td>
                <td>Unlimited</td>
                <td>Unlimited</td>
                <td>No</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>IRA/Roth IRA</td>
                <td>$1.36M+ (2022)</td>
                <td>$1.36M+ (2022)</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>SEP/SIMPLE IRA</td>
                <td>Unlimited</td>
                <td>Unlimited</td>
                <td>No</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Life Insurance</td>
                <td>No</td>
                <td>Varies</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody></table>
        
        <div class="warning-box">
            <h3>⚠️ Important Timing Considerations</h3>
            <p>Asset protection strategies must be implemented BEFORE trouble arises. Transfers made after creditor claims arise may be considered fraudulent conveyances and can be reversed by courts.</p>
        </div>
        
